# Line endings are part of this project's contract, not a platform preference:
#   * command.txt and spec/*.tsv must be LF so the POSIX and Windows implementations parse byte
#     -identical input (tests/encoding.ps1 enforces this).
#   * bin/dsh-os.bat must be CRLF with no BOM; cmd.exe mis-parses it otherwise.
#   * bin/dsh-os.ps1 must be CRLF and is committed as UTF-8 with BOM (encoding.ps1 enforces it).
#
# `text=auto` normalizes to LF inside Git's object store, and the per-pattern eol= settings decide
# what a checkout writes. Using `-text` here instead would mark every file binary, which silently
# overrides the eol= lines below and checks out an LF .bat that cmd.exe cannot parse.
* text=auto

*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.tsv text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
